== 3. PC direct baseline: TLS vs phase0 plaintext ==
method deviation: PS/.NET (schannel) is 100% RST'd by the middlebox above -> Go crypto/tls client
(scratchpad tlsbase, Proxy=nil DIRECT, ForceAttemptHTTP2=false, keep-alive reuse like phase0), same shape:
echo x22 drop 2 warmup + default 100-token stream (40tps nominal, 25ms grid).
  first request (TCP+TLS1.3 handshake + echo): 229.6ms  proto=HTTP/1.1
  echo RTT (n=20): min=11.1ms p50=12.0ms p95=13.3ms jitter(p95-p50)=1.2ms
  phase0 plaintext reference (20260712): min=22.8 p50=28.1 p95=45.5 jitter=17.3
  NOTE: p50 12.0 vs 28.1 — network conditions differ across days/route; NOT attributable to TLS
  (TLS adds a handshake, it does not lower steady-state RTT). Steady-state echo over an established
  TLS connection shows no measurable penalty vs plaintext era.
  stream: headers=12.8ms first_read=12.8ms total=2489.5ms reads=102 tokens=100 summary=true
  inter-read gaps: n=101 p50=25.1ms p95=26.4ms coalesced(<1ms)=2 stalls(>200ms)=0 (nominal 25ms)
  phase0 plaintext reference: p50=25.1 p95=29.2 coalesced=2 stalls=0 -> pacing fidelity unchanged under TLS.

